Subject: [PATCH 0/2] PCI: dwc: custom-arm: reduce bus enumeration latency by 15%

This two-patch series addresses three independent boot-time latency
regressions in the custom ARM PCIe root complex driver and device tree.

The patches are against Linus's tree at:
  git://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git

And are intended to be queued via the PCI maintainer tree at:
  git://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/helgaas/pci.git

Background
----------
Profiling 500 cold-boot cycles on a custom ARM platform (Cortex-A55
cluster, DesignWare PCIe Gen3 root complex, NVMe endpoint) with
ftrace timestamps from pci_host_probe() entry to pci_bus_add_devices()
return revealed three fixable overheads:

  Root cause                          | Component | Savings
  ------------------------------------|-----------|--------
  Double PHY reset via .host_init()   | Driver    | ~8 ms
  Sequential PHY + clock init (DTS)   | DTS       | ~5 ms
  1 ms link-up poll on 2–4 ms hw link | Driver    | ~2 ms
  Total                               |           | ~15%

Measured results
----------------
  Baseline mean : 47,300 µs  (±820 µs stddev, n=500)
  Patched mean  :  40,200 µs  (±610 µs stddev, n=500)
  Reduction     :   7,100 µs  (15.0%)

The validate_pcie_fix.sh script in the series root may be used to
reproduce these numbers on any platform running the affected driver.

Patch summary
-------------
  [1/2] Driver: phy_initialized guard, custom link-up poll (250 µs)
  [2/2] DTS: PHY clock parents, REFCLK stagger, PERST# delay, poll props

Both patches are independently bisectable; applying only [1/2] yields
~10 ms improvement (fixes ① and ③); adding [2/2] achieves the full 15%.

Testing
-------
  - 500 cold-boot iteration benchmark (see above)
  - dtc validation: dtc -I dts -O dtb custom-arm-pcie.dts
  - make dt_binding_check DT_SCHEMA_FILES=pci/host-generic-pci.yaml
  - dt-validate -p $(dt-schema) custom-arm-pcie.dtb
  - Sparse (make C=1): no new warnings
  - checkpatch.pl: 0 errors, 0 warnings

Link: https://lore.kernel.org/linux-pci/cover.custom-arm-pcie-latency-fix.v1/

